  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Prior Approval for change of use from Class E to residential use providing 1 self contained residential unit including internal refuse and cycle stores.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Prior approval is required Under Schedule 2, Part 3, Class MA of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2016. The Council has determined that prior approval is hereby REFUSED as it is considered that there is no indication that the outbuilding has been within one or more of the classes specified in sub-paragraph (2) for a continuous period of at least 2 years prior to the date of the application for prior approval. As such, the outbuilding that has not been in use previously for Class E use and cannot be converted to residential use under Prior Approval.",
    "Given the proximity of the railway and the Carshalton United (FC) ex-service club, and without evidence to the contrary through a noise and vibration impact assessment (with details of noise insulation and mitigation measures necessary to achieve the BS 8233:2014 standards), the proposal would result in an adverse impact on the noise levels within the proposed residential unit to the detriment of future occupiers' amenity and is therefore contrary to criteria (d) of Class MA.",
    "The proposal would fail to provide adequate natural lighting to all habitable rooms within the new residential unit, with the rear bedroom being particularly affected. The proposal would therefore result in a poor living standard for future occupiers and is contrary to criteria (f) of Class MA."
  ],
